# M-tiling / transpose baseline
#
# The four is_transa/is_transb combinations at a shape that spans multiple
# M-tiles (has_m_loop_, non-literal m_loop). m_tiles is also the regression
# case for the eager-ptrb M-tile-base stack-coalescing bug (fixed by giving
# eager B its own variable_t(pointer_t) slot); the transA=1 case covers the
# runtime-lda mul/nb_tmp_ path in the M-tile-base update.
--reset
--transA=0,1 --transB=0,1
64x8x16_n"m_tiles"

# Scaling sanity: bigger than the baseline group (more M-tiles, larger N/K),
# untransposed and transposed-A+B, to catch anything that only shows up once
# the dense loops actually iterate more than a couple of times.
--reset
96x12x24_n"larger_square_untransposed"

--reset
--transA=1 --transB=1
96x12x24_n"larger_square_transab"

--reset
128x16x32_n"large_untransposed"

# M == VLMAX exactly: a single M-tile, but still through the has_m_loop_
# (non-literal m_loop) path rather than a literal single-tile path.
--reset
16x4x8_n"single_m_tile"
